# Deliberately narrow. This repository has core.autocrlf=true on the owner's machine, which
# is fine for source — but the three files below are parsed line-by-line by Netlify rather
# than by a compiler, and a stray CR is the kind of thing that makes a rewrite rule quietly
# not apply. A missing rewrite does not break navigation inside the app; it breaks refresh
# and pasted links only, which is a failure nobody notices until someone else hits it.
#
# CI checks out on Linux and would get LF regardless. This is for a local build that is
# ever deployed by hand.
#
# NOT a whole-repo normalisation on purpose: CRLF working copies are also what the
# edge-function byte-for-byte verification is calibrated against (see CLAUDE.md — compare
# with `diff --strip-trailing-cr`), and renormalising everything would rewrite that
# comparison's baseline for no benefit.

public/_redirects text eol=lf
public/_headers   text eol=lf
netlify.toml      text eol=lf
